From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:53:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: take down the partners of an AP MLD owner and
 re-enable them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

027 removes the BSSes of other interfaces that run on the driver of an
interface that is being removed or disabled, but only when that
interface's first BSS is a plain BSS. An interface whose first BSS is
itself an AP MLD link kept upstream's semantics: hostapd_cleanup_driver()
sees the driver shared with the partner links, removes only the departing
link and leaves the driver, its nl80211 context and the netdev to them.

On prplOS with pWHM that is the common topology. The MLD netdev is the
main VAP of the radio that came up first (wlan0.1), and the first BSSes
of the other radios are links of it that borrow its context. When pWHM
re-applies such a radio with a configuration in which that VAP is no
longer an AP MLD link, it sends REMOVE for the owner interface and ADDs
the new configuration, and the ADD initializes a new driver on the same
netdev while the surviving context still holds the wdev's management
frame registrations:

  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan0.1_link0'
  hostapd: Configuration file: /tmp/wlan0_hapd.conf (phy wlan0) --> new PHY
  hostapd: nl80211: kernel reports: Match already configured
  hostapd: nl80211: Could not configure driver mode
  hostapd: nl80211 driver initialization failed.
  hostapd: Adding interface bss_config=wlan0 failed
  wld: wlan0: warm apply failed to add iface conf => restart to recover

cfg80211_mlme_register_mgmt() rejects a match that another socket has
already registered on the wdev with -EALREADY, and pWHM recovers with a
full hostapd restart. If instead the last partner link goes away later,
the driver stays allocated with drv->ctx pointing at a freed
hostapd_data and the next interface-down event on that netdev is
delivered to it.

Drop the AP MLD exclusion in hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(): what
matters is that the driver behind bss[0] was created by this interface,
which hapd->drv_owner_iface records. The partners are taken down before
the driver cleanup, so that hostapd_cleanup_driver() finds the driver
unshared, deinitializes it and releases the netdev, and the ADD gets a
fresh driver.

A partner that is the first BSS of its interface is disabled, keeping
its configuration and control sockets. For an AP MLD owner it is also
marked mld_partner_disabled, and when a later interface setup completes,
hostapd_mld_reattach_partners() runs from the event loop and enables
every marked interface whose AP MLD has a running first BSS with a
driver again: driver_init() borrows the new context as before and the
interface setup runs on the unchanged configuration. So a REMOVE/ADD of
the owner alone, with the same AP MLD, brings such partners back
without any controller action.

An explicit DISABLE of the interface, including one that is already
down, or its REMOVE cancels the pending re-enable, and the timer is
cancelled once nothing is pending. The eviction itself uses an internal
disable that does not cancel it.

Known loss: a partner that is a secondary BSS of another, running
interface is removed with hostapd_remove_bss(), as 027 does for a plain
owner. Its configuration is freed and it comes back only when the
controller supplies it again, e.g. with pWHM's AP MLD configuration
refresh or a REMOVE/ADD of that radio; an owner-only re-apply with an
unchanged AP MLD does not restore it. Likewise, if the owner comes back
as a plain BSS or with another AP MLD, a disabled first-BSS partner
stays down until the controller re-applies it.

A plain first BSS owner keeps 027's handling unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 162 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/ap/hostapd.h |  10 +++
 2 files changed, 168 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index d4e66426e2f5..044b08df9bf9 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -70,6 +70,12 @@ static void hostapd_cleanup_unused_mlds(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces);
 static int hostapd_remove_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface, unsigned int idx);
 static void hostapd_interface_setup_failure_handler(void *eloop_ctx,
 						    void *timeout_ctx);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+static void hostapd_mld_reattach_partners(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx);
+static bool hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces);
+static void hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(struct hostapd_iface *iface);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+static int hostapd_disable_iface_int(struct hostapd_iface *hapd_iface);
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AX
 static void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handler(void *eloop_data,
 						 void *user_ctx);
@@ -2830,6 +2836,19 @@ dfs_offload:
 	if (iface->interfaces && iface->interfaces->count > 1)
 		ieee802_11_set_beacons(iface);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* This interface may have given an AP MLD a first BSS with a driver
+	 * again; let the partners hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers() disabled
+	 * borrow it. Do it from the event loop, outside of this setup. */
+	if (iface->interfaces &&
+	    hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces)) {
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+				     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+		eloop_register_timeout(0, 0, hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+				       iface->interfaces, NULL);
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	return 0;
 
 fail:
@@ -3546,6 +3565,109 @@ hostapd_interface_init_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces, const char *phy,
 }
 
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+static bool hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces)
+{
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		if (interfaces->iface[i] &&
+		    interfaces->iface[i]->mld_partner_disabled)
+			return true;
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* An explicit disable or removal of the interface cancels its pending
+ * automatic recovery: it stays down. */
+static void hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	if (!iface->mld_partner_disabled)
+		return;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Interface %s: cancel pending AP MLD partner recovery",
+		   iface->phy);
+	iface->mld_partner_disabled = 0;
+	if (iface->interfaces &&
+	    !hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces))
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+				     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+}
+
+
+static struct hostapd_data *
+hostapd_mld_running_first_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+			      const char *mld_name)
+{
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->mld_count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_mld *mld = interfaces->mld[i];
+
+		if (mld && os_strcmp(mld->name, mld_name) == 0 && mld->fbss &&
+		    mld->fbss->drv_priv &&
+		    mld->fbss->iface->state == HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED)
+			return mld->fbss;
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+
+/**
+ * hostapd_mld_reattach_partners - Re-enable the interfaces disabled for a
+ * departed AP MLD owner once their AP MLD has a first BSS again
+ * @eloop_ctx: struct hapd_interfaces *
+ * @timeout_ctx: Not used
+ *
+ * hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers() disables an interface whose first BSS is an
+ * AP MLD link borrowing the driver of an AP MLD owner interface that goes
+ * away and marks it mld_partner_disabled. Once a first BSS of the same AP
+ * MLD runs again with a driver of its own, such an interface can borrow that
+ * context as it did before: enable it, which runs driver_init() and the
+ * interface setup on its unchanged configuration. An explicit disable or
+ * removal clears the mark (hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery()).
+ */
+static void hostapd_mld_reattach_partners(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx)
+{
+	struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces = eloop_ctx;
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+		struct hostapd_data *hapd;
+
+		if (!iface || !iface->mld_partner_disabled || !iface->num_bss)
+			continue;
+
+		hapd = iface->bss[0];
+		if (iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_DISABLED || hapd->drv_priv ||
+		    !hapd->conf->mld_ap) {
+			/* Enabled meanwhile: nothing to do */
+			iface->mld_partner_disabled = 0;
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		if (!hostapd_mld_running_first_bss(interfaces,
+						   hapd->conf->iface))
+			continue;
+
+		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+			   "Re-enable interface %s: the AP MLD it borrows its driver from has a first BSS again",
+			   hapd->conf->iface);
+		iface->mld_partner_disabled = 0;
+		if (hostapd_enable_iface(iface))
+			wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+				   "Failed to re-enable interface %s",
+				   hapd->conf->iface);
+	}
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
+
 /**
  * hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers - Remove the BSSes of other interfaces that
  * run on this interface's driver
@@ -3565,6 +3687,21 @@ hostapd_interface_init_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces, const char *phy,
  * a context takes its whole interface down (DISABLE) instead. The BSSes are
  * identified by drv_owner_iface, which does not depend on the first BSS of
  * the MLD or the first BSS of the driver still being present.
+ *
+ * When the first BSS of the departing interface is itself an AP MLD link,
+ * the driver is shared with the partners, and upstream would leave it, its
+ * nl80211 context and its netdev to them. That keeps the netdev busy: the
+ * mgmt frame registrations of the surviving context stay on its wdev, a later
+ * ADD of that interface fails to initialize a new driver on it
+ * (NL80211_CMD_REGISTER_FRAME: -EALREADY, "Match already configured"), and
+ * once the last partner link is removed the driver survives with drv->ctx
+ * pointing at a freed hostapd_data. Take the partners down in this case too,
+ * so that hostapd_cleanup_driver() finds the driver unshared and frees it. A
+ * first-BSS partner disabled for an AP MLD owner is marked
+ * mld_partner_disabled and re-enabled by hostapd_mld_reattach_partners()
+ * once its AP MLD has a first BSS with a driver again. A secondary partner is
+ * removed with its configuration, as for a plain owner, and comes back only
+ * when the controller supplies it again.
  */
 static void hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 {
@@ -3572,8 +3709,7 @@ static void hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces = iface->interfaces;
 	size_t j, k;
 
-	if (!interfaces || !iface->num_bss || !iface->bss[0]->drv_priv ||
-	    iface->bss[0]->conf->mld_ap)
+	if (!interfaces || !iface->num_bss || !iface->bss[0]->drv_priv)
 		return;
 
 	for (j = 0; j < interfaces->count; j++) {
@@ -3589,7 +3725,10 @@ static void hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 				   "Disable interface %s: its first BSS uses the driver of %s that is being deinitialized",
 				   other->bss[0]->conf->iface,
 				   iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
-			hostapd_disable_iface(other);
+			if (hostapd_disable_iface_int(other) == 0 &&
+			    iface->bss[0]->conf->mld_ap &&
+			    other->bss[0]->conf->mld_ap)
+				other->mld_partner_disabled = 1;
 			continue;
 		}
 
@@ -3662,6 +3801,9 @@ void hostapd_interface_deinit_free(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s(%p)", __func__, iface);
 	if (iface == NULL)
 		return;
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(iface);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(iface);
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s: num_bss=%u conf->num_bss=%u",
 		   __func__, (unsigned int) iface->num_bss,
@@ -3800,7 +3942,7 @@ int hostapd_reload_bss_only(struct hostapd_data *bss)
 }
 
 
-int hostapd_disable_iface(struct hostapd_iface *hapd_iface)
+static int hostapd_disable_iface_int(struct hostapd_iface *hapd_iface)
 {
 	size_t j;
 	const struct wpa_driver_ops *driver;
@@ -3856,6 +3998,18 @@ int hostapd_disable_iface(struct hostapd_iface *hapd_iface)
 }
 
 
+int hostapd_disable_iface(struct hostapd_iface *hapd_iface)
+{
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* Also when the interface is already down, e.g. taken down by
+	 * hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(): it must stay down. */
+	if (hapd_iface)
+		hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(hapd_iface);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+	return hostapd_disable_iface_int(hapd_iface);
+}
+
+
 static struct hostapd_iface *
 hostapd_iface_alloc(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces)
 {
diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.h b/src/ap/hostapd.h
index 27674652600e..fbb1399c8da1 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.h
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.h
@@ -598,6 +598,16 @@ struct hostapd_iface {
 	 */
 	unsigned int driver_ap_teardown:1;
 
+	/*
+	 * Pending AP MLD partner recovery: set by hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers()
+	 * when this interface was disabled because its first BSS borrowed the
+	 * driver of an AP MLD owner interface that went away.
+	 * hostapd_mld_reattach_partners() enables it again once its AP MLD has
+	 * a first BSS with a driver again; an explicit disable or removal of
+	 * this interface clears it.
+	 */
+	unsigned int mld_partner_disabled:1;
+
 	/*
 	 * When set, indicates that this interface is part of list of
 	 * interfaces that need to be started together (synchronously).
